course: dictionary
lesson: 14389
title: Swinging back and forth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe movement that goes back and forth again and again. Oscillate is one of them. When you meet it, look for clues in the words around it. «The pendulum of the old clock began to oscillate, swinging left and right.» A pendulum swings, and left and right show it moves in two directions, so oscillate means swinging back and forth.
explain: Oscillate can also describe feelings or ideas that keep changing. «Ben's mood would oscillate between hope and fear as he waited for the results.» Ben does not feel one thing for long. He moves from hope to fear and back again. Look for the word between, because it shows there are two things the feeling moves between.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The fan on my desk oscillates.» Try "The fan on my desk swings back and forth." It still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Oscillate means to swing or move back and forth regularly.
fact: A pendulum, like the one in a grandfather clock, is a classic example of something that oscillates.
fact: Oscillate can also mean to keep changing between two feelings, ideas or states, as in «oscillate between hope and fear».
fact: In science, electric current and waves can oscillate, changing direction or strength in a regular rhythm.
fact: Oscillate is a verb: oscillates (now), oscillated (before), oscillating (happening now).
exercise: «The fan on my desk oscillates from side to side.» What does oscillates mean here? | Makes a loud noise | Gets very hot and then stops | Stays still and does not move | *Swings or moves back and forth
exercise: Ella's feelings oscillate between excitement and worry before the test. What does this show? | She is sleepy and keeps yawning | *She keeps changing back and forth between two feelings | She has stopped feeling anything at all | She is always happy
exercise: «The pendulum of the old clock began to oscillate.» Which word from the list means about the same as oscillate? | Sleep | Freeze | *Swing | Shout
test: The electric current in the wire will oscillate, changing direction many times each second. What does oscillate mean in science? | Stops flowing completely | *Changes direction and strength in a regular rhythm | Turns into light and sound | Gets hotter and hotter until it glows
test: Sam's mood would oscillate between hope and fear while he waited. Which pair of feelings does oscillate describe? | Happy and sleepy | Hungry and full | Loud and quiet | *Hope and fear, changing back and forth
exam: Which sentence uses oscillate correctly? | I will oscillate my homework to the teacher tomorrow | She oscillated a happy song across the room | *The pendulum began to oscillate, swinging left and right | The cake began to oscillate in the oven and went golden
